<title>AUSTRALIA: AUSTRALIA'S NRMA SAYS ENTERS HOME LOAN MARKET.</title>
<headline>AUSTRALIA'S NRMA SAYS ENTERS HOME LOAN MARKET.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1997-08-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Unlisted Australian motoring and insurance group, the National Roads and Motorists Association (NRMA), said on Monday it has entered the home loan market.</p>
<p>The group said it would offer a Home Value variable home loan with an interest rate set at 6.35 percent.</p>
<p>NRMA financial services general manager Lester Doecke said in a statement that the home loan market was extremely competitive, but the group was used to operating in markets with tight margins and would benefit from customer loyalty.</p>
<p>-- Sydney Newsroom 61-2 9373-1800</p>
</text>
